{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/pulls/18","id":4279630433,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTWpA987_Ffph","html_url":"https://github.com/open-hax/katamorph/pull/18","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-hax/katamorph/pull/18.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-hax/katamorph/pull/18.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/issues/18","number":18,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(condition): require portable safe-integer path indices","user":{"login":"riatzukiza","id":10676925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjc2OTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10676925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza","html_url":"https://github.com/riatzukiza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/riatzukiza/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Scope\n\nAdd reusable `PortableInteger` semantics for exact safe integral values and use that primitive for numeric Condition path segments instead of unrestricted `int?`. Boundary tests prove ±(2^53−1) are lawful and ±2^53 are rejected. A finite safe JVM Double with an integral value is accepted because it is the same portable value as ClojureScript's single Number representation; non-integral doubles remain ordinary portable numbers, not path indices. Runtime path validation uses the same law and converts an already bounded vector index before `nth`.\n\n## Provenance-preserving reconciliation\n\nExact integration commit `db6853576876d05c30178ad09e951ce46f9bd0be` has tree `f591f5253f0b01c1b593e609f2c5f30a142d4256` and parents:\n\n- original PR head `a8be789605f8e4266398bdfbadf06def22e72be4`;\n- exact `main` `8e0b3b12ce94a04eca81a2d27697939d8cfb04c0`.\n\nAn independent `git merge-tree` reproduction yielded the same integration tree. No original history was rewritten.\n\nThe current exact successor is `54ca5bc83146358646eb93b4ee99e750ca3e0fb8` with tree `d72ab00f845701553396c68e1e7baecc5d10007e`.\n\n## Cold-run and review repairs\n\n- Integrated lint found two unused test refers and one redundant single-string `str`; the repair leaves full clj-kondo at 0 errors / 0 warnings.\n- First exact-head Sandbox ran JVM tests, examples, and build, then truthfully failed two CLJS assertions because JavaScript cannot distinguish source `1.0` from integral `1`.\n- Fresh Codex review correctly identified the deeper P1 consistency defect: the test-only adjustment still left identical values with different schema/runtime behavior across CLJ and CLJS.\n- The semantic repair accepts finite safe integral JVM Doubles, shares `PortableInteger` with runtime path lookup, converts bounded vector indices before `nth`, and adds Byte/Short/Integer/Long coverage requested by independent eta review.\n- A later exact Codex review caught the stale diagram edge that still rejected integer-valued Double; the successor routes CLJ integral values and CLJS integral Numbers through the same boundary.\n- A later exact Codex review found JVM map lookup still distinguished Long `1` from Double `1.0`; path-side normalization closed that direction.\n- The next exact review proved one-sided normalization reversed the mismatch for Double-keyed maps. Numeric traversal now canonicalizes both map keys and path segments, and fails closed on ambiguous JVM-only canonical collisions.\n- A stale independent review claimed CLJS rejects `-0.0`; exact ClojureScript 1.12.145 source disproves that premise, so no semantic churn was made.\n- Automatic exact-head CodeRabbit then found safe JVM `BigInt` representations were excluded. The repair uses value-based `integer?` plus direct safe-bound comparison and adds `5N` coverage.\n- Exact eta/MiMo found no blocking defect and requested direct coverage of ambiguous JVM numeric-key collisions. A JVM-only regression now proves traversal fails closed.\n\nAll eight review threads are answered with exact evidence and resolved. CodeRabbit independently inspected `c56c051` and confirmed its BigInt finding is addressed; the only descendant change is the eta-requested collision regression and its receipt.\n\n## Validation\n\n- RED hosted Sandbox CLJS: **198 tests / 584 assertions**, 2 failures exposing the original expectation error;\n- RED JVM for the semantic repair: **70 tests / 288 assertions**, 3 failures covering integral-Double schema, condition shape, and vector lookup;\n- RED JVM for path-side numeric map normalization: **70 tests / 289 assertions**, 1 failure;\n- RED JVM for symmetric numeric map normalization: **70 tests / 290 assertions**, 1 failure;\n- RED JVM for safe exact `BigInt`: **70 tests / 291 assertions**, 1 failure;\n- GREEN JVM: **70 tests / 292 assertions**, 0 failures or errors;\n- GREEN exact-head hosted Sandbox [run 33284619926](https://github.com/open-hax/katamorph/actions/runs/33284619926): JVM **70 / 292**, CLJS **198 / 587**, examples and release build all successful;\n- GREEN full clj-kondo: **0 errors / 0 warnings**;\n- `git diff --check`, `git fsck --full --no-dangling`, exact ancestry, and merge-tree identity passed;\n- Receipt River parses as **31 EDN forms**.\n\nLocal CLJS remained blocked before project load by the expired Maven proxy. The exact test-only successor passed the hosted JVM/CLJS/examples/build gate, fresh Codex completed clean, fresh eta/MiMo approved with no findings, and CodeRabbit's implementation finding was confirmed fixed on its code-bearing parent.\n\n## Merge contract\n\nMerge only if the head remains exact, hosted checks are truthful and green, fresh exact-head Codex and substantive eta/MiMo review are clean, CodeRabbit confirms its BigInt finding on the successor, and every review thread is resolved.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added consistent portable-integer validation across JVM and JavaScript runtimes.\n  * Path conditions now support safe integer values, including exact integral decimals within the supported range.\n  * Numeric map keys and vector indexes are handled consistently across equivalent integer representations.\n  * Ambiguous numeric map matches are reported as missing instead of producing uncertain results.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a workflow diagram explaining numeric validation, path handling, and cross-runtime behavior.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Expanded coverage for safe-integer boundaries and numeric path compatibility.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-08-14T12:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T01:06:27Z","closed_at":"2026-08-30T01:06:27Z","merged_at":"2026-08-30T01:06:27Z","merge_commit_sha":"7a754b751eb2ea5ff8ecba42986b04e35a0537c1","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/pulls/18/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/pulls/18/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/issues/18/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-hax/katamorph/statuses/54ca5bc83146358646eb93b4ee99e750ca3e0fb8","head":{"label":"open-hax:fix/portable-safe-integer-paths","ref":"fix/portable-safe-integer-pat